<!doctype html><html lang="en-CA"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><title>Programs | PictureThis Production</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"/></head><body><a href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a href="/"><b>PICTURETHIS PRODUCTION</b></a><nav><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/programs/">Programs</a><a href="/faithfire/">Faithfire</a><a href="/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/blog/">Blog</a><a href="/events/">Events</a><a href="/partners/">Partners</a><a href="/get-involved/">Get Involved</a><a href="/donate/">Donate</a></nav></header><main id="main"><section><h2>Programs</h2><p></p></section><section><h2>Training</h2><p>An eight-week course, Saturdays 10:00 AM to 2:00 PM, at Faithfire Production, 139 Millwick Dr, and partner venues across the GTA. Cables and signal flow in week 1; a full production crewed by the cohort in week 8.</p></section><section><h2>Mentoring</h2><p>Every participant is paired with a working technician: someone who mixed, switched or lit a show this month. Monthly check-ins at minimum, help with first bookings, rates, and when to say no.</p></section><section><h2>Pathways</h2><p>First bookings are usually cable and stagehand calls, then operating positions. We don't promise you a job. We promise hands-on time with real gear, honest instruction, a reference from people the industry knows, and a crew that'll say your name when a call comes in.</p></section><section><h2>Production Management</h2><p>The other half of putting on a show: advancing the event, building the run sheet and call sheets, managing the budget, and calling the show on the day. Participants who work well on a crew learn to run the production, not just handle one role in it.</p></section><section><h2>Technical Management</h2><p>For those who go on to lead a department: planning the rig, choosing and maintaining the gear, signing off on safety, and teaching the next cohort. It's the top of the pathway, the people who spec out the room and are accountable for it.</p></section><section style="overflow-x:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Session — what you actually do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Wk 1</th><td><strong>Cables, connectors and signal flow</strong><p>Coil, tape and test every cable type we own. Follow a signal from microphone to speaker and find the break we hid in it.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 2</th><td><strong>Digital consoles: the Wing and X32</strong><p>Build a show file from empty: inputs, gains, EQ, routing, scenes. The two consoles most GTA rooms actually run.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 3</th><td><strong>Mixing a live band</strong><p>Soundcheck a real band at Faithfire. Vocals first, then everything else. Learn what to do when it feeds back anyway.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 4</th><td><strong>Cameras and video switching (ATEM)</strong><p>Frame, focus and follow. Then sit in the director's chair and call a two-camera rehearsal on comms.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 5</th><td><strong>Lighting: rigging safely, running a desk</strong><p>Hang, focus and cable a rig without hurting anyone. Program cues and run a service from the lighting desk.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 6</th><td><strong>Streaming, lyrics and media (ProPresenter)</strong><p>Build a full service file: lyrics, scripture, sermon slides, stream output. Advance it live, on the director's call.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 7</th><td><strong>Show calling, comms and event etiquette</strong><p>Call a show start to finish. Comms discipline, dress codes, client manners — the conduct half of the job.</p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wk 8</th><td><strong>Capstone: crew a real production</strong><p>A full event, crewed entirely by the cohort, mentors on comms only if needed. This is the reference you graduate with.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></section></main><footer><p>Training: Faithfire Production, 139 Millwick Dr, Toronto.</p><p>PictureThis Production is being set up as a nonprofit organization in Ontario.</p><p>Faithfire Production is its production arm.</p><a href="/policies/">Our standards & policies</a> · <a href={"mailto:"+contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a> · Placeholder contact</footer></body></html>